1. Executive Summary & System Architecture
To build a valid digital cognitive engine, the application must capture two distinct vectors of user data: Behavioral Performance Metrics (active interactions measuring response latency, precision, and sustained attention) and Psychometric Self-Reports (structured questionnaires measuring habituation, environmental factors, and perceived cognitive load). Combining these vectors ensures the app doesn't just evaluate what users think they do, but how their brains perform under active execution demands.
The app architecture uses a modular schema, enabling individual test modules to pipe their raw scores into a centralized Profile Aggregation Engine. This engine processes the metrics across three foundational pillars:
