2. Domain 1: Attention Dynamics & Executive Functioning (ADHD Risk Markers)
This module adapts the principles of the traditional Continuous Performance Test (CPT) into an engaging mobile/web layout. The goal is to isolate the user's baseline attention profile by evaluating three distinct types of errors: Commission Errors (impulsivity markers), Omission Errors (inattention/distractibility markers), and Reaction Time Variability (neurological consistency markers).
2.1 Interactive Task Specification: The Digital Go/No-Go Engine
The interface displays a rapid succession of geometric shapes centered on a clean background. Users must tap the screen as fast as possible when a "Go" target arrives and explicitly withhold actions when a "No-Go" target appears.
Target Stimulus (Go): Solid green circle. Frequency: 80% of total trials (establishes a strong prepotent motor response loop).
Nontarget Stimulus (No-Go): Solid red circle or green triangle. Frequency: 20% of total trials (requires active executive inhibition).
Inter-Stimulus Interval (ISI): Variable pacing at 1000ms, 1500ms, and 2000ms blocks to prevent rhythm-based predicting. Stimulus display duration is fixed at 400ms.
Total Duration: 3 minutes (120 total trials).
