3. Domain 2: Information Processing, Memory Mechanics & Learning Styles
This module diagnoses how a user's sensory and cognitive systems encode, retain, and recall information. It moves past generic "learning styles" to evaluate concrete, measurable performance profiles across different sensory inputs, matching them with targeted self-reported study habits.
3.1 Interactive Task Specification: The Multi-Modal Digit-Span Engine
The system runs two distinct tests to measure working memory capacity limits across visual and auditory pathways.
Visual Forward Digit-Span: Random numeric sequences appear on screen one character at a time for 800ms, followed by a 200ms blank screen. The user must type the exact sequence in forward order using an on-screen keypad. The sequence starts at a length of 3 numbers and grows by 1 number every time the user answers correctly twice in a row. The test stops when the user misses two consecutive attempts at the same length.
Auditory Backward Digit-Span: The system plays audio clips of distinct numbers spoken at 1-second intervals. The user must enter the sequence in reverse order. This variant evaluates structural manipulation within the working memory space.
