4. Domain 3: Cognitive Load Tolerance & Problem-Solving Strategies
This module evaluates fluid intelligence, executive flexibility, and performance under time pressure. It tracks how efficiently a user adapts when task rules change suddenly, measuring cognitive switching costs.
4.1 Interactive Task Specification: The Rule-Switching Matrix Task
A playing card or graphic asset drops into the center of the display. The asset has three variable features: Number (1, 2, or 3 symbols), Color (Cyan or Magenta), and Shape (Star or Diamond).
The Dynamic Rule: The top header displaying the active sorting rule changes every 5 rounds without warning (e.g., alternating between "SORT BY COLOR" and "SORT BY SHAPE").
User Response Mechanism: Two targets sit at the bottom of the screen. Users tap the target that matches the active rule.
Primary Metric Captured: Switching Latency Cost. The system calculates the average reaction time increase on the first two rounds after a rule change compared to the final two rounds of the previous rule.
4.2 Post-Task Subjective Mental Workload Scale (NASA-TLX Framework)
Immediately after the rule-switching matrix task, the user adjusts sliders graded from 0 (Extremely Low) to 10 (Extremely High) to rate their internal mental effort.
