5. Algorithmic Scoring, Profile Aggregation & Claude-Code Directives
This section contains the math engine formulas and the implementation instructions needed to build a functional code parser.
5.1 Mathematical Scoring Mechanics
To calculate a clean Attention Divergence Risk Score (ADHD Risk Vector ranging from 0 to 100), the backend engine uses the following multi-variable equation:
Score = [ (Commission_Errors / Total_NoGo) * 35 ] + [ (Omission_Errors / Total_Go) * 35 ] + [ (Normalized_ASRS_Score / 24) * 30 ]
Where Normalized_ASRS_Score is the sum of points from questions ATTN-01 through ATTN-06, considering only responses that meet or exceed the designated threshold value.
